{
  "configuration_id": "config_026",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, scgpt+imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) scored 0.507 acc / 0.455 F1, while config_002 (RNA-only, scgpt, transformer) scored 0.514 acc / 0.498 F1. The multimodal model underperforms its RNA-only counterpart, suggesting the concat fusion may be forcing equal-weight integration of potentially noisy image features. Question: config_026 isolates a single change—switching fusion from concat to weighted—while keeping scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, and transformer aggregation identical to config_001. This tests whether learned modality weighting can recover the performance gap and determine if the image modality is salvageable. Why this is the best next step: With 7 experiments remaining, we need to resolve whether the multimodal pipeline is worth further investment or whether we should pivot to RNA-only improvements. A single-variable change (fusion only) gives the cleanest causal signal about the integration strategy, directly informing whether subsequent experiments should explore other image encoders/aggregations or focus on the RNA side."
}

